# crowdlock-churn: crowdlock (the standing crowd of the audited 18-hour game on its real ground, 246 bodies, 147
# fight-moves; see crowdlock.scn) while the map changes: one 1x1 feature in the crowd's own area, closing no way, is
# placed and lifted every 300 ticks, as buildings, wrecks and corpses change a real game's map all the time (the
# audited game did). Each change refreshes the routes it touches, and the stall clock's record is re-based to where
# the body stands: a body one step back from its best place then read its next step forward as a gain, and the
# dead age of its whole knot restarted. Four bodies (the 4x4 and 3x3 doorway pair and two queued on them) held
# their orders for good, at tick 20,000 as at 9,000; every order now ends, the last at tick 7,528.
# Keys (with --scale): scale.complete.n (147; 143 before), scale.stuck_end and open_still900 (0; 4 and 3 before).
# The types are the install's (data-gated).
